(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[5 1 "// Attribute lookup (PY5c; CPython's _PyType_Lookup, PyObject_GenericGetAttr and SetAttr,"] [6 1 "// type_getattro and type_setattro): data descriptors before the instance's __dict__, non-data"] [7 1 "// descriptors after; the built-in types' attributes (tp_getset, tp_members) as GetSets beside their"] [8 1 "// dictionaries, and their slots seen as methods (slot wrappers) as CPython's add_operators puts them"] [9 1 "// in the type's dictionary."] [11 1 "// GetSet is a built-in type's attribute (getset_descriptor): Get, and Set (nil: read-only; v nil:"] [12 1 "// delete)."] [18 2 "// member: a PyMemberDef's attribute, member_descriptor where CPython has one (types.MemberDescriptorType is"] [19 2 "// type(FunctionType.__globals__)); read-only ones say \"readonly attribute\""] [21 2 "// shared: 3.15's one __dict__ or __weakref__ descriptor of every class (object's; queue 237), its repr without"] [22 2 "// an owner"] [37 1 "// AddGetSet declares a built-in type's attribute."] [48 1 "// AddMember declares a built-in type's PyMemberDef attribute."] [54 1 "// AddMethod puts a built-in method in a built-in type's dictionary (bound to the instance by"] [55 1 "// attribute lookup: fn gets the instance first)."] [60 1 "// AddToDict puts v in a built-in type's dictionary once the runtime is ready (a dictionary's keys"] [61 1 "// are hashed by str's slot, which an init function may run before)."] [80 1 "// readyDataModel completes the built-in types' dictionaries, once."] [96 1 "// lookupAttr is _PyType_Lookup over t's MRO: each type's dictionary, its GetSets, and for a built-in"] [97 1 "// type its slots as slot wrappers; the value and the type it was found on."] [120 1 "// The type attribute cache (PY6-core, queue 200, after PY8's measurement: lookupAttr was 31-35% of a run;"] [121 1 "// CPython's method cache over tp_version_tag): each type keeps its lookups' answers by name, the absent ones"] [122 1 "// too, and drops them all when typeEpoch moves. typeEpoch moves on any change to a type's namespace (the dicts"] [123 1 "// marked ofType: an insertion, a replaced value, a deletion, a clear, popitem), on a getset added, and on an"] [124 1 "// MRO set (c3MRO's and readyTypes'), so an answer is never older than the namespaces it was read from."] [132 1 "// lookupAttrMRO is _PyType_Lookup's walk: t's MRO's dicts, then the getsets and slot wrappers of each."] [153 1 "// superLookup is lookupAttr over the part of start's MRO after typ (super's lookup)."] [182 1 "// descrGet is a found attribute's __get__ (obj nil: from the class); a built-in method found on a"] [183 1 "// built-in type is bound to obj (its value for a built-in subclass's instance)."] [189 3 "// object's methods take the instance itself (PY6d's REQUEST: __reduce_ex__'s class); objectDescr is"] [190 3 "// methodDescrs[b] == ObjectType without the map's lookup on every method's binding (queue 210)"] [202 1 "// methodDescrs are the built-in types' methods that left their type's dict through the class (T.name: CPython's"] [203 1 "// method_descriptor), each with its type: put in a class's dict (socket.socket.getsockname = saved, test_socket's"] [204 1 "// test_injected_authentication_failure) such a method still binds to the instance, as a method descriptor does,"] [205 1 "// where a built-in function there (class A: f = len) does not."] [210 1 "// instanceDict is o's __dict__, nil when it has none."] [246 1 "// The attribute instructions' inline caches (202b; PEP 659's LOAD_ATTR and STORE_ATTR caches, after the type"] [247 1 "// version tag): load-attr and store-attr of an object whose type takes the generic path keep, per instruction, the"] [248 1 "// type they last saw and lookupAttr's answer for it, valid while typeEpoch has not moved (the epoch the type"] [249 1 "// attribute cache's own answers hold by, attr.go's lookupAttr), so a hit compares two words where lookupAttr hashes"] [250 1 "// the name into the type's cache."] [256 2 "// di: where the instance's dict held the name when it was last found there (queue 210; CPython's"] [257 2 "// LOAD_ATTR_INSTANCE_VALUE's index): an entry holding the name's very str (co_names are interned) is the name's"] [261 1 "// lookupAttrAt is lookupAttr(tp, name) through the cache of c's instruction pc."] [267 1 "// attrSite is an instruction's caches: the last types it saw, the latest first (queue 210: richards' four task"] [268 1 "// classes share their methods' instructions, and one entry missed at every change of type)."] [273 1 "// attrICAt is c's instruction pc's cache entry holding lookupAttr(tp, name)."] [295 34 "// tp's old entry, else the oldest, dropped"] [300 1 "// dictEntryAt is the position of the entry of d holding name itself, through the hint *di (kept up to date); -1"] [301 1 "// when d does not hold name (an equal str in its place is found, but not kept as the hint)."] [313 1 "// loadAttrAt is load-attr at c's instruction pc: GetAttr, its generic path's lookup through the instruction's cache."] [322 3 "// genericGetAttrFound's instance dict through the hint (queue 210)"] [344 1 "// storeAttrAt is store-attr (v nil: delete-attr) at c's instruction pc: SetAttr, its generic path's lookup through"] [345 1 "// the instruction's cache."] [354 3 "// genericSetAttrFound's dict.Set through the hint: a value replaced in place (queue 210)"] [363 21 "// the usual case: the name inserted last"] [370 1 "// GenericGetAttr is object.__getattribute__."] [377 1 "// genericGetAttrFound is GenericGetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [395 1 "// GenericSetAttr is object.__setattr__ (v nil: object.__delattr__)."] [402 1 "// genericSetAttrFound is GenericSetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [430 1 "// typeGetAttr is type.__getattribute__: the metatype's data descriptors, then the type's MRO, then"] [431 1 "// the metatype's other attributes."] [444 29 "// a method descriptor leaving its type"] [452 4 "// a built-in type's class and static methods know their type for __qualname__"] [475 1 "// typeSetAttr is type.__setattr__: a class's attribute, its slots updated for a special one."] [486 3 "// tp_name: a static type's module and name ('compression.zstd.ZstdCompressor'; builtins' bare)"] [506 1 "// SetAttr is setattr(o, name, v); v nil is delattr."] [514 1 "// DelAttr is delattr(o, name)."] [517 1 "// GetAttrOptional is getattr(o, name) with nil, not an AttributeError, when there is no such attribute."] [520 1 "// LookupSpecial is a special method's lookup on o's type (_PyObject_LookupSpecial): bound to o, or nil."] [529 1 "// getAttrOptional is getattr(o, name, None) without the None: nil when there is no such attribute."] [541 1 "// callBound calls a method found on self's type bound to self (CPython's vectorcall of an unbound"] [542 1 "// method with self first, or __get__ then the call); owner is the type of self's MRO it was found on"] [543 1 "// (lookupAttr's), nil when not known."] [550 4 "// wrapperdescr_call's check (bpo-37619: a wrapper of the wrong class in a class's dict)"] [556 4 "// a built-in function in a class's dict is no method descriptor: called without the instance, as"] [557 4 "// descrGet's rule and lookup_maybe_method (class C: __call__ = len; typing.NewType's __call__ = _idfunc,"] [558 4 "// queue 207)"] [562 4 "// object's own methods take the instance itself (descrGet's rule, PY6d's R2), as for"] [563 4 "// object.__reduce_ex__ of a class deriving from a built-in type (PY6g's F2: random.Random's pickling)"] [619 2 "// a descriptor's own attributes (PY6a: inspect's getattr_static reads __name__ and __objclass__)"] [635 2 "// object's attributes"] [637 2 "// a built-in type with a dictionary shows it itself (BaseException's, function's, module's); a class's is"] [638 2 "// subtype_getsets_full's, in the dict of the class that adds it (addLayoutDescrs): object has none"] [646 2 "// BaseException's attributes (exceptions.c's BaseException_getset and members)"] [705 1 "// unpackAll is the items of an iterable."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[67 32] [71 32] [110 31] [137 31] [141 28] [145 35] [157 6] [157 20] [163 9] [163 23] [166 31] [170 28] [174 35] [185 26] [196 33] [281 23] [303 18] [321 27] [329 41] [353 27] [355 21] [359 32] [362 34] [383 28] [406 34] [440 33] [441 27] [455 34] [459 34] [464 34] [481 35] [497 38] [508 32] [570 33] [591 18] [688 58]]} (go/file "attr.go" :imports [

